From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stubbyfowl <sidaksmann@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:34:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix: retire the SAMtools/BCFtools SNP caller

The SAMtools caller runs

    samtools mpileup -uD ... | bcftools view -ceg ...

which is samtools/bcftools 0.1.x syntax. Every bcftools on bioconda
(1.2-1.24) rejects `view -ceg` ("Could not parse --min-ac eg"), and the
0.1.19 bcftools bundled with old samtools reads a different file format
than samtools 1.x writes, so it silently produces no calls. The option
could only ever yield empty VCFs.

Retire it the same way the SolSNP caller was retired:
- the interactive prompt is commented out and the intro now lists the
  callers that work (GATK and VarScan);
- a config file that still names a SAMtools caller is skipped with a
  clear message instead of launching a job that produces nothing.

_run_samtools is left in place for whoever ports it to `bcftools call`.
GATK and VarScan are unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 nasp/dispatcher.py | 10 ++++------
 nasp/nasp.py       | 19 ++++++++++---------
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/nasp/dispatcher.py b/nasp/dispatcher.py
index a0fa900..1b0a8d8 100755
--- a/nasp/dispatcher.py
+++ b/nasp/dispatcher.py
@@ -573,12 +573,10 @@ def _call_snps(aligner_output, configuration, reference):
                     if job_id:
                         snpcaller_output.append((vcf_nickname, job_id, final_file, aligner_name, name))
                 elif re.search('samtools', name, re.IGNORECASE):
-                    (vcf_nickname, job_id, final_file) = _run_samtools(nickname, bam_file, snpcaller,
-                                                                       configuration["samtools"],
-                                                                       configuration["job_submitter"], aligner_job_id,
-                                                                       reference, configuration["output_folder"])
-                    if job_id:
-                        snpcaller_output.append((vcf_nickname, job_id, final_file, aligner_name, name))
+                    # Retired: _run_samtools uses samtools/bcftools 0.1.x syntax (mpileup -uD | bcftools view -ceg)
+                    # that no packaged bcftools accepts, so it can only produce empty calls.
+                    print("The SAMtools/BCFtools SNP caller is no longer supported (use GATK or VarScan). Skipping...")
+                    logging.warning("SNP caller '%s' skipped: the SAMtools/BCFtools caller is no longer supported" % name)
                 else:
                     print("Unknown SNP caller \'%s\' found, don't know what to do. Skipping..." % name)
     return snpcaller_output
